     "result_text_tail": "target as $40M by 2032.\n\n**Decisions I made in your absence** (each is listed in the deck's appendix and open to challenge):\n- **$40M ambition:** I read it as a 2030 revenue target. If the board meant \"a trajectory toward $40M\", A may already satisfy it.\n- **Retail revenue:** counted at the $14 wholesale price Onsoo receives, not the $28 shelf price.\n- **Cash:** pre-tax and undiscounted, with inventory held at four months of landed cost.\n- **Tariff stress:** the 25% duty is applied to all four years, which is conservative.\n- **My own proposals:** a $4M cash envelope, an ad-cost guardrail of 28% or less, and a retail trigger of 20% aided awareness. The CEO's 15% trigger is too low: at 10\u201320% awareness the median brand still falls below the delisting level.\n- **File format:** I delivered PowerPoint (editable) plus a PDF copy. Charts are drawn as shapes, not linked chart objects.\n\n**How I checked it:** the sandbox blocked Chrome and Quick Look, so I couldn't open the deck in PowerPoint. I previewed every slide with a small renderer I wrote using macOS's own text engine, fixed overlaps, overflows and one wrong number, and produced the PDF with the same renderer. It should match closely, but spacing in PowerPoint may differ slightly, so flip through the PowerPoint file once before it goes to the board.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- `Onsoo_US_Entry_Board_Deck.pptx`\n- `Onsoo_US_Entry_Board_Deck.pdf`\n- `source/` (the model and build scripts; rerun them to regenerate every figure)"
